# Link Masker

Create random share links that redirect to your real URLs.

## Run it
```bash
npm install
ADMIN_KEY=choose-a-secret npm start      # Windows PowerShell: $env:ADMIN_KEY="choose-a-secret"; npm start
```
Open http://localhost:3000, paste a URL, click **Create masked link**, copy and share.

## Settings (environment variables)
- `ADMIN_KEY`: only people with this key can create/list/delete links (visitors don't need it)
- `BASE_URL`: your public address, e.g. `https://links.yourdomain.com`, so copied links use it instead of localhost
- `PORT`: default 3000

## Deploy
Any Node host works (Render, Railway, Fly.io, a VPS). Note: links are saved in `links.json`, so use a host with a persistent disk, or swap in a database.